**Given:**

First 17 natural numbers

**Formula used:**

Average of squares of first n natural numbers = dfrac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6n}

**Calculation:**

n = 17

⇒ dfrac{17(17+1)(2×17+1)}{6×17}

⇒ dfrac{17×18×35}{102}

⇒ dfrac{10710}{102}

⇒ 105

**∴ The correct answer is 105.**

Concept used:

Sum of the first N natural numbers = frac {N(N+ 1)}{2}

Calculation:

Sum of the first 60 natural numbers = frac {60(60 + 1)}{2}

Now, the average of the first 60 natural numbers = frac {60(60 + 1)}{2} div 60 = 30.5

**∴ The average of the first 60 natural numbers is 30.5.**
